  "description": "meme-id: the_pope_says_trump_is_not_a_christian_because_christians_dont_build_walls_vatican_walls_are_40_feet_high; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes an image of Pope Francis with a quote attributing to him that 'Christians don't build walls,' then contrasts this with an image of Donald Trump at a podium and a photo of the high walls of the Vatican, implying that Trump's wall-building is inconsistent with Christian values. The intent is to mock or criticize Trump by suggesting his actions contradict the Pope's stated beliefs. While not explicitly targeting a protected group with hate, it is harmful because it misrepresents the Pope's position, potentially inciting division or disrespect toward religious authority, and uses a religious figure to make a political point in a way that could be seen as disrespectful or misleading. The meme relies on a false equivalence between the symbolic, spiritual nature of the Vatican walls and the political, physical nature of Trump's proposed border wall, which is a form of misleading argumentation that can contribute to polarization.",
